    fix(dogfood): scratch-HOME hygiene checker + checklist/diag updates (DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-27)
    
    A previous dogfood run redirected HOME into /tmp/dogfood-tj and left
    home/.bunker/config.yaml (mode 644) holding a live bunkerd token: a scratch HOME
    that receives a credential file turns /tmp into a key store. The leak was purged
    and the token rotated on the host; this commit lands the repo-side guard.
    
    - scripts/scratch-home-hygiene.sh: scans a root (default /tmp) for dogfood-*
      scratch dirs and flags those readable beyond their owner (any group/other bit)
      that hold a credential-shaped file — matched by file name (config.yaml,
      config.yml, *.env, *token*, *secret*, *credential*) or by a credential
      assignment line in the content. Exits 1 on a finding, 0 when clean, 2 on a bad
      scan root. Prints paths and mode strings only: matched contents are tested with
      `grep -q` and never echoed.
    - tests/test_scratch_home_hygiene.py: pins the contract — a clean root exits 0, a
      0755 dir with a world-readable config.yaml fails, the same file under 0700 is
      suppressed by tight perms, the fixture credential value never reaches
      stdout/stderr, and the content branch stays independent of the name branch.
    - docs/dogfood/checklist.md: standing item — scratch trees under /tmp/dogfood-*
      are created 0700 and never receive credential files; run the checker at the end
      of every dogfood tick and treat a non-zero exit as a pre-closure blocker.
    - docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md: resolution paragraph for the §8.6 scratch-dir
      hygiene section (purge plus rotation, and the checker + checklist item as the
      structural guard). No credential values or secret paths are recorded.
    
    Verification: the checker exits 0 on this host's /tmp (24 scratch dirs, 0
    findings); .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_scratch_home_hygiene.py -x
    --tb=short -> 7 passed; full suite -> 1348 passed, 7 skipped; gitreins guard
    tier 1 PASS (secrets/lint/tests/static_analysis).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
